# ACOS Operating Spine v1.2 — Changelog

**Issued 2026-09-03. Supersedes v1.1 (2026-09-02), which superseded v1.0 (2026-09-01).**
Produced in response to `57-second-redteam-remediation.md`. Scope: apply all **22 BLOCKING (T1)** findings from the narrow second independent red team. No production code, no schemas, no repository, no vendor provisioning.

---

## 1. What v1.2 is

The second red team returned **CONDITIONAL PASS — zero FATAL, 22 BLOCKING, 24 MATERIAL, 6 MINOR, 4 WORDING**, with 10 constructed attacks defeated by the v1.1 design as written. v1.2 applies all 22 BLOCKING items: **15 APPLIED**, **7 APPLIED WITH EXPLICIT RESIDUAL**, **0 NOT APPLIED**. Every residual is a named, bounded consequence recorded in an artifact rather than an unresolved defect.

Two authority-boundary escapes drove the CONDITIONAL verdict, and both are closed:

- **Path A — headroom laundering.** An `I32` starvation override released reservations, refilled the window, changed no signed quantity and therefore fired no re-signature, multiplying realisable refund loss while the owner believed they were answering a liquidity question.
- **Path B — self-declared degraded mode.** The control plane decided when it was degraded, and degradation *relaxed* the dispatch rule for clock-bearing effects. The audited party chose when the audit applied.

## 2. The shape of the v1.1 defects

v1.1's arithmetic was independently reproduced and found correct in all ten figures (`54 §2.1`). What v1.1 got wrong was **semantics**, and one pattern accounts for most of it:

> **A quantity or threshold a mechanism needs, that the artifact declaring quantities does not declare.**

`min()` against an undeclared window cap. An `I3` "window ceiling" that existed in no artifact. A 30-day basis against a calendar-month window. A `boundary_kind` never stated. A canonical serialisation never specified. A `cessation_lag` never measured. Each was invisible to review because each read as complete prose.

The second pattern is **an invariant asserting a property it does not entail** — `I18`'s three-way equality between quantities that are unequal whenever a cost component exists, and four citations of `I31` for a property `I31` does not state. Registry check **C5b (entailment)** is new in v1.2 for exactly this.

## 3. Changes by finding group

### R1 / Canonicaliser — SR-C1..C4

`I18` **retired**, replaced by `I18a`–`I18d` over a split `exposure { vendor_amount (nullable), total_exposure }`. Per-action caps now compare against `total_exposure`, so a $25.00 refund carrying a $1.03 retained fee **denies**. `enumerate_effects` becomes a named, journaled, `context_spec`-filtered, rate-limited READ capability with an `EnumeratedOptionSet` return type. Selectors become content-addressed `(enumeration_id, option_id)` pairs; the kernel **never substitutes** (I53). Constructors gain a `ConstructorVersionRecord` and become control-artifact class 19; `ACOS-JCS-1` becomes class 20.

### R2 / Standing — SR-S1..S4

Every window declares `boundary_kind`; **all nine production windows are DISCRETE** and ROLLING is defined but `NOT_ADMISSIBLE_AT_MVP`. Five-state machine with a declared transition table; forward exposure retained in **every non-`REVOKED` status**; `REVOKED` requires cessation verification (I54) and is **structurally unavailable at MVP** because `cessation_lag` is `UNMEASURED`. `StandingRevocationAuthority` (I55) resolves the pause deadlock. Forward exposure moves to the **exposure-remainder** form.

### R3 / Audit — SR-A1..A6

`I17` restated as **transport** completeness; the unqualified claim moves to `I8`. `JournalAttestation` at 5-minute cadence, k=3, new `I17e`. Three-state mirror machine in which the uncorroborated state is **stricter** (new `I17f`, two-sided). `ACOS-JCS-1` canonical serialisation. `journal_counter` row allocator with a declared lock order. Idempotent re-push. The five-row halt table becomes an **ordered first-match precedence list**.

### R8 / Limits — SR-L1..L4

`max_monetary : Money | UNBOUNDED`, **not nullable**. Grants narrow; the window binds. `window_balance` rows with a `CHECK` under `FOR UPDATE` replace the unimplementable exclusion constraint. Order-driven irrecoverable cost becomes a fifth displayed quantity and a seventh exclusion (I57). `PRESUMED_SETTLED` closes Path A.

### R9 + R17-P4 — SR-R1..R4

Reservation TTL derives from the tier SLA; OWNER reservations exempt from reaping. Seven-state Approval machine with a unique partial index on `RESUMING` (I60). `RemedyObligation` (I58). `settlement_direction` becomes **`value_direction`** with six values; P4 restated over three outbound values; **P8** added for `INTERNAL_LIABILITY`. Hand proof extended to **22 classes, five explicit exclusions and a P6 reachability column**. New `I51`, DB-enforced.

## 4. Deliberate deviation from the remediation spec

**One.** `57 §2` SR-S4 specifies `rate × remaining_periods × (1 + overdelivery_allowance)`. Under a $6.00/day rate in a 31-day January with $12.00 of documented day-1 overdelivery, that form computes `12 + 29×6 = 186 > 180` and **the campaign still pauses on day 2** — the attack the finding was raised to close. v1.2 uses `forward = max(0, standing_cap − realised)` with `standing_cap(MONTH) = rate × max(days_in_window, monthly_basis_multiplier)`, which re-reserves at exactly $186.00 and does not pause. Recorded in the ledger under SR-S4 and raised as question **B8** of the third brief.

## 5. New identifiers

`I17e`, `I17f`, `I18a`–`I18d`, `I51`–`I61`. `I18` retired. Registry totals: **68 identifiers, 55 MVP / 13 excluded, 22 audit-owned, 21 DB-enforced** (enumerated by name in `phase2-v1.2-invariant-registry.md §2.8`).

